  "Windows' default Sleep (Modern Standby) sometimes drains the battery from background wake-ups or fails to resume cleanly. Hibernate saves the session to disk and fully powers off, which is closer to how SteamOS suspends and tends to be more reliable - at the cost of a slightly slower resume. Setting the Power Button and Hibernate Timeout options above to Hibernate (and disabling Windows' Sleep timer) is the recommended change.": "Windows 默认睡眠（Modern Standby）可能因后台唤醒耗电，或无法正常恢复。休眠会将会话保存到磁盘并完全关机，与 SteamOS 的挂起方式更接近，通常更可靠，但恢复稍慢。上游建议将电源键与自动休眠选项设为休眠，并关闭 Windows 睡眠计时。",
